  "interpretation": "Every bound uses only the count conserved within each booking. With all members known, one false negative and one false positive can be repaired together. For unknown predictions we take the minimum and maximum over all possible original positive counts, allowing them to absorb swaps. Subscope no-harm counts permit swaps with other known mistakes, and are independent maxima, not additive. Gross fixes allowing harms may displace a correct passenger; they are not accuracy gains.",
